	(text "GATE INPUTS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "09c2dc3f-246d-525e-9515-63da98220a2d")
	)
	(text "Adapted from Ogham's clock input (Ogham feeds the comparator's − input; this one is non-inverting, so four channels\nshare one threshold divider): 10 kΩ, BAT54S clamps to +3V3D / GND, 100 kΩ to ground, LM393 against GATE_TH = 1.65 V with\n100 kΩ hysteresis. Trips at ≈1.98 V rising, ≈1.67 V falling at the jack. The LM393 runs from +12 V so the clamped\ninput (up to ≈3.6 V) stays inside its common-mode range (VCC − 1.5 V; at 5 V that would be 3.5 V). Open-collector\noutput pulled up to +3V3D: GATE_INn is high while the gate is high, safe for any module. Firmware: catch 100 µs\ntriggers with edge interrupts or PIO. The clamps push up to ≈3.4 mA into +3V3D: the 680 Ω minimum load on the\npower sheet absorbs it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3add26ef-ab4e-5c5f-af61-ddfe0e6ff69e")
	)
